    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0174" n="68" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg68"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Pacheco</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wharton acknowledges Mr. Pacheco’s telegram of the 10th instant and calls his
                    attention to Department’s telegram of the same date. He is <pb facs="0175"
                        n="69" xml:id="pg69"/> instructed to protest against any arbitrary actions
                    by the authorities of Salvador toward the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">City
                        of Panama</hi>, even if vessel has been seized, which would not affect
                    instructions previously sent him. A full report of the facts is asked for.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
